nd post-restart recovery verification, including a final live DHCP renewal on node3 after all three reboots.","actions_performed":["Mapped topology: node1 bridges two isolated segments via eth1 (172.20.1.0/24, node2 side) and eth2 (172.20.2.0/24, node3 side)","Installed Kea DHCPv4 on node2, configured subnet4 172.20.2.0/24 with relay ip-addresses 172.20.2.1, bound to enp8s0","Upgraded openssl-libs on node2 to fix a symbol lookup error that prevented kea-dhcp4 from starting","Installed and enabled isc-dhcp-relay on node1 with INTERFACES='eth1 eth2' SERVERS='172.20.1.2'","Set node2's enp8s0 to a persistent static IP (172.20.1.2/24) via nmcli and added a static route 172.20.2.0/24 via 172.20.1.1 to fix misrouted DHCPOFFER replies","Opened firewalld 'dhcp' service (UDP/67) permanently on node2's public zone","Persisted node1's eth1/eth2 addressing via /etc/network/interfaces.d and forwarding sysctls via /etc/sysctl.d/99-antrieb.conf","Verified node3 (NetworkManager, DHCP auto on enp8s0) obtained lease 172.20.2.124/24 with gateway 172.20.2.1 from node2's Kea server through node1's relay","Captured baseline boot IDs and service/data health on all three nodes","Rebooted node1 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot ID, verified relay/addressing/forwarding recovery, and confirmed node3 could still renew its lease","Rebooted node2 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot ID, verified kea-dhcp4/static IP/route/firewall/lease-data recovery, and confirmed node3 could still renew its lease","Rebooted node3 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot ID, and verified it automatically re-acquired its DHCP lease from node2 via node1's relay","Final consolidated health check across all three nodes post full restart cycle"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node3 obtains its DHCP address from node2's service across separate segments of node1","command_ids":["cmd-daa860ca94e44637","cmd-db6e691f40394445","cmd-14a465c6bb